invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_verify
reason: the host verifier compares r with the x of a sum at infinity. The
  sum's coordinates are then zero, and X == r * Z^2 holds, so the verifier
  accepts a pair whose u1*G and u2*Q are negatives, which is no signature.
  The proof requires the verdict 0 when the infinity test answers 1, and
  its stub of the comparison requires a finite sum; the cases of
  bin/p256_verify_equiv_test whose R is the point at infinity fail too.

--- old
    if (p256_wide_jacobian_is_infinity(&sum)) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
